.DS_Store
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.pyc

# Every hidden entry beside the published stores is a build's working state,
# never a dataset: scripts/pinned_build.py stages a store as
# .stage.<id>.zarr, sets the replaced one aside as .<id>.zarr.backup-<token>
# and holds .<id>.zarr.publish.lock while it publishes, and cellucid.prepare()
# writes .<name>.<pid>.partial before it moves a store into place. One of them
# surviving a run means an interrupted build, which is resolved by rerunning the
# builder; committed, a stage or a backup would publish a complete second copy
# of a dataset that the catalog never names.
/anndata/.*

# Tool caches (pytest, mypy, ruff, pytest-benchmark)
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.benchmarks/

# Scratch directories a crashed publisher test can leave behind
.pinned-publish-test-*/
